So the fix: track whether a comma was actually seen. Also `{% set x = 1, %}` → `(1,)` as well (renders `(1,)`). And empty tuple with explicit parens works, but `{% set x = %}` should fail with "Expected an expression". Let me check the current behavior of that:

Current: `{% set x = %}` → parse_tuple: explicit_parentheses False, current block_end not rparen. Loop: is_tuple_end → block_end → True → break immediately. items empty. `len(items)==1` false → return nodes.Tuple([], "load") — an empty tuple without parens, which upstream would reject with a syntax error "Expected an expression".

